# RR2c-1 (critical_qualifier_receivers_bug; steps/qualifier-receivers-20261010.md; the author's example of 2026-10-10,
# LMX_blog/2026-10-10.md#qualifier-receivers-20261010): a merge operand written as a typed declaration without
# parentheses, `merge(Integer  int: value newValue)`, is an anonymous Structure of that one field -- P0 gives the atom
# and the Frame as two actuals -- built where the merge runs, its candidate a declaration's: a formal, an expression, a
# literal, fields of earlier results.  By name and type it takes the model's slot; first (`merge(int: value 9; Other)`)
# it is the model, and a later operand's same-name field goes into its slot.  Exit 7; 81..85 name the failing merge.
Integer:
    int: value 0
end: Integer
Other:
    int: w 2
end: Other
Over:
    int: value 5
end: Over
fn: getInteger (int: newValue) int
    a: merge(Integer  int: value newValue)
    return: a\value
end: getInteger
fn: m () int
    if: getInteger(7) != 7
        return: 81
    b: merge(Integer  int: value 2 + 3)
    if: b\value != 5
        return: 82
    c: merge(int: value 9; Other)
    if: c\value * 10 + c\w != 92
        return: 83
    d: merge(int: value 9; Over)
    if: d\value != 5
        return: 84
    e: merge(Integer  int: value b\value + c\value)
    if: e\value != 14
        return: 85
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
